# 🗂️ Verification evidence stays local, period.
#
# Every run under benchmarks/results/ used to be committed — raw tool output,
# config copies, environment dumps, and later the summaries themselves. That
# is where incidental personal detail kept turning up (an ACME account
# address, EC2 instance ids, hostnames of the owner's machines), so as of
# 2026-08-03 the whole tree is excluded from the repository. The SHA256SUMS
# in each directory still lets a privately archived raw tree be verified
# byte-for-byte, and the conclusions are published in benchmarks/README.md.
benchmarks/results/

# 📋 Planning documents are working material, kept local.
#
# TODO.md tracks known-but-unfixed weaknesses day by day, including
# reproducible ones in already-released code. A public, prioritised list of
# your own unpatched defects is a target list; publish the fix, not the queue.
#
# SITE.md is the website plan. Same shelf for the same reason plans belong
# there: they contradict themselves as facts arrive, and a plan read as a
# promise is worse than no plan. Publish the site, not the sketch of it.
#
# STATUS.md is the verification ledger: which public claim has evidence
# behind it and which does not. The second half of that sentence is the
# problem — a list of the claims we cannot currently back is a list of the
# places to push on. Publish the verified claim, not the ledger.
#
# TRIAGE.md is the same shelf for the same reason, and it is the sharpest
# case: a triage row is at its most useful when it names the exact input
# that breaks something, so a good row is a working reproduction for a
# defect that is by definition still unfixed. AGENTS.md and
# docs/GUARDRAILS.md may say the inbox exists and how to use it — the
# method is fine to publish. The inbox is not.
#
# docs/refactor/ holds the split queue and the agent prompts driving it,
# including commit-ratio and per-file defect-density figures. Working
# material about how the work gets done, and unflattering out of context.
docs/TODO.md
docs/SITE.md
docs/STATUS.md
docs/TODO_CADDYFILE*.md
TRIAGE.md
docs/refactor/
/.plan-snapshots/
# 🧹 The same two notes also exist as loose copies at the repository root.
# Ignored by name so a stray `git add -A` cannot publish what the entry
# above was written to keep local.
/pingclair-claude-code-prompts.md
/pingclair-split-queue-and-usage.md

